## Loop rules (short version)

1. Nothing ships without a devil's-advocate review.
2. Strict file ownership per implementation agent — no two agents on the same file
   in the same cycle.
3. Implementation agents run **no git commands** — the orchestrator commits.
4. Project test gate green before every push: `<TEST COMMAND — e.g. "npx vitest run">`.
5. Small, clean commits. No force-push. No merge without the human.
6. A maintainer stop is final until a new explicit go.

